# A unit-level constant reading an element or member a data block does not
# have is the body's error for the same read. It was refused as a construction,
# which named the wrong mistake. An element of a block whose elements are a
# typedef'd record still builds a value, and is still refused as a construction.
byteid: typedef u8

primes: data { 2 3 5 7 }
ids: data {
    first: 1
} out byteid
PAST: primes.9
NAMED: primes.nosuch
BUILT: ids.first

main: function is {
    print "\{PAST} \{NAMED}"
    b: BUILT
}
